### Dummy muonic X-ray spectrum, to check the atomic cascade: mu- stopped directly in a target of one
### material, one job (scripts/dummy_xray.sh runs one per material and cascade model). The target is
### the 20 x 20 x 1 cm box of macro/geom_target_al.mac (centre at z = 36 cm) with its material
### replaced. Needs the aliases dummyMaterial (NIST name, e.g. G4_Al, G4_Si), dummyModel
### (firstPrinciples or geant4, /tof/physics/muonCascade), dummySeed, dummyEvents, dummyDir, dummyFile.
### Every event is one mu- of 1 keV started at the centre of the target: that is the lowest kinetic
### energy Geant4 tracks a muon at, so it stops where it starts and every event is a stop in the
### target. A gun run has no live time: the analysis gives everything per stopped mu- (the yield).
### Every event is written (/EventFilter 0), so the stops are counted exactly, also those without any photon.

/control/execute macro/geom_target_al.mac
/tof/target/material {dummyMaterial}
/update
/tof/physics/muonCascade {dummyModel}

/OutputFormat 1
/EventFilter 0
/OutputDirectory {dummyDir}
/OutputFile {dummyFile}
/gun/seed {dummySeed}
/GeneralParticleSource 0
/gun/particle mu-
/gun/energy 1 keV
/gun/position 0 0 36 cm
/gun/direction 0 0 -1
/run/beamOn {dummyEvents}
